03 · P0 / P1 status by LOB — one table per 主類別 in tracker order: # · Item · Owner · Status · Derived · Evidence (one clause naming where you saw it, linked) · Next. Every P0 exactly once. P2 only if OVERDUE. Cells ≤12 words — this is a scan surface, not a narrative. Where the tracker and another source disagree, say which wins under precedence and put the reconciliation in Next.
04 · Per-owner summary — one line per owner (named as the tracker names them): P0 · P1 · UNDATED · OVERDUE · ENDS_SOON · what the brief needs from them · when they last appeared in the weekly log. End with `GM holds <k>/<n> P0s (<pct>%)`.
05 · KPI off-target + missing numbers — (a) Off target: rows with BOTH a target and an Actual where the Actual misses the current quarter's target; (b) Missing: rows with no Actual → metric · owner · how it would be filled; CRM/accounting-backed ones marked `(not readable on a scheduled run)`. Batch by owner.
06 · Decisions register — table: id · Item · Label (`已定案` / `還在摸索` / unlabelled) · Decider · decide-by (or "no deadline") · Status · Source (linked). Sources: 待決事項 rows (all, open first); DIRECTION_UNLABELLED P0s; the two known strategy-level open decisions if not already listed (course platform: build vs use an existing one, pending cohort ROAS; B2C high-ticket vs shifting to B2B) marked "no deadline" unless a date exists. The three promoted into 01 appear here too, marked `→ see 01`, so the register stays whole.
07 · Deliberately not this week — 3–5 named skips (e.g. P0s scheduled to start later — protect the date, don't half-start; items whose owner is out; P1/P2 with no date pressure) with one clause each.
08 · Machine health — livestream-curation last date (+ flag); SOR docs changed in the last 7 days (or "modifiedTime not exposed — skipped"); sources unavailable in this cloud run (CRM · accounting · calendar); tab-level deep links unavailable (Drive connector exposes no gid); DEAD REFERENCES — any `[N.N]` code or `§` section named by a source that resolves to no real document; the idempotency result; `STALLED detection pending P1`.
One-line focus for the subject: the single most important thing from block 01, in plain English, ≤10 words, naming the thing at stake rather than its code. Good: `4 pricing decisions are 3 days overdue`. Bad: `§D 決策逾期 3 天`.
BEFORE YOU RENDER, run this check and rewrite anything that fails: (1) does every 01 card ask ONE question ending in a question mark? (2) could the reader answer it without opening another document? (3) does every card give real options, or the exact value and cell? (4) is every document, sheet and tab named anywhere in the brief a hyperlink? (5) is there a `[N.N]` code, `§` reference or acronym that is never expanded? (6) is any dead reference passed off as a citation instead of reported in 08? (7) read block 01 aloud — does it sound like a person telling you what they need?

